Moreover she added a certain one whose name I’m unwilling to speak, lest he uplift his red eyebrows. He is a lanky fellow, against whom some time ago was brought a grave law-suit over the spurious child-birth of a lying belly.
I cannot conceal, goddesses, in what way Allius has aided me, or with how many good services he has assisted me, lest the flight of time through ages of forgetfulness cover with night’s blindness this care of his.
But I shall tell it to you, and you in time to come declare it to many thousands, and make this paper, grown old, speak of it And let him be more and more noted when dead, nor let the spider aloft, weaving her thin-drawn web, carry on her work over the neglected name of Allius. For you know what anxiety of mind twofold Amathusia gave me, and in what manner she overthrew me, when I was burning like the Trinacrian rocks, or the Malian fount in Oetaean Thermopylae;

for there he is; go, you stub-horned one, and say: Milon,
even Proteus, though a god, pastured his seals.
May I not have the land of Pelops, nor talents of gold
to possess, nor to outrun the winds;
but under this rock will I sing, holding you in my arms,
watching the flocks graze together, toward the Sicilian sea.
For the trees winter is a dread evil, for the waters drought,
for the birds the snare, for the wild beasts the net,
for a man the longing for a tender maiden. O father, O Zeus,
I am not the only one to have loved; you too love women.
So the boys sang in answering strains;
and Menalcas led off the last song in this way.
Spare my kids, wolf, spare my mothers,
and do me no wrong, though I am small and tend so many.
O Lampurus, my dog, are you held by so deep a sleep?
